title: "AI Foundations | Continuation Boundary"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-20"

authors:
  - family-names: "Solen"
    given-names: "Alyssa"

abstract: "Defines the AI Foundations Continuation Boundary: the point at which a later state ceases to provide evidence of continuation because the particular structure of the prior trajectory no longer makes a discriminable difference to the production or direction of the future state. The repository separates preservation from continuation and specifies a counterfactual evaluation design for locating boundary crossings under controlled perturbation."

